==English==
{{wikipedia|Epistolary}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|en|e|pis|to|la|ry}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪˈpɪst(ə)ˌləɹi/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-epistolary.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Etymology 1===
1650s, from {{bor|en|fr|épistolaire}}, from {{der|en|la|epistolārius}}, from {{m|la|epistola||letter}} (English {{m|en|epistle}}) + {{m|la|-ārius}},<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> from {{der|en|grc|ἐπιστολή}} from {{m|grc|ἐπιστέλλω||I send a message}} from {{m|grc|ἐπί||upon}} + {{m|grc|στέλλω||I prepare, send}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Of or relating to [[letter]]s, or the [[writing]] of letters.
# Carried on by [[written]] [[correspondence]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''epistolary''' relationship}}
# In the manner of written [[correspondence]].
#: {{ux|en|'''epistolary''' style}}
#: {{ux|en|an '''epistolary''' novel}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=297|volume=II|passage=But Sir Jasper has a great talent for '''epistolary''' correspondence—to be sure he has nothing else to do; but my time is of great importance.}}

